* ''A single operator's re-found reads idempotent by intent'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-31: //"As git holds all history & refounding for a single operator reads idempotent by intent (we can freely tear down identity & costs at any time), we need this goal added to the overall roadmap. Combine the road/roadmap & reprioritize with these adds."//). While one operator holds the mesh, a re-found tears identity down freely: git holds the history, so a teardown costs nothing git cannot restore, and the same rites land the same house shape again under fresh keys. A re-found runs the way the fresh start runs, by hand and reversible, never through a pave or wipe command (#/fresh-start). It narrows no standing ruling, and the house reads it beside them: the fence holds, so the shape cuts land before the second operator seats a key and a re-found stays cheap until her pins depend on it (#/rulings, the fence); the live test still runs with two operators from its first day; after `X0` a re-genesis costs every CID a second operator pins (#/stride-3-bake), while a single operator's identity re-found before her seat costs nothing; old shapes still burn, so a format cut re-founds and no source reads pre-cut bytes (#/rulings, the fresh start). `X0b`'s idempotent-by-intent pass sweeps the code a re-found replays, and the memory stage keys its memes so a re-pour reproduces them (`L9`).

